[UTCTime "13:49:37"]

{ The knight's pawn poses extra difficulties, but the key squares still win. We just need to be slightly more careful. }
3. Kg6 { The winning technique is to move our king to the other side of the pawn to avoid stalemating the black king on h1. } (3. Kf6 Kh7 4. Kf7 Kh8 { Kf6 does not lose our advantage, but forces us to repeat back into the starting position. }) 3... Kg8 4. Kh6 (4. Kf6 Kf8 (4... Kh7 5. Kf7 Kh8) 5. g6 Kg8 6. g7 Kh7) 4... Kh8 5. g6 Kg8 6. g7 Kf7 7. Kh7 *


