[UTCTime "13:54:34"]

{ For a pawn on the fourth rank, the key squares are still those of the pawn on the 5th. For a pawn on the 2nd or 3rd ranks, the key squares are two ranks above the pawn. } { [%csl Gc6,Gd6,Ge6] }
5. Kd5 (5. Ke5 Ke7 6. Kd5 Kd7 7. Kc5 Kc7 { Ke5 is a mistake, as it allows black to draw with opposition. } 8. d5 Kd7 9. d6 Kd8 10. Kc6 Kc8) 5... Ke7 6. Kc6 { We reach one of the key squares and win as seen previously. } 6... Ke8 7. d5 Kd8 8. Kd6 Ke8 9. Kc7 *


