8. Kb1 { Here we can successfully defend with distant opposition, which is when both kings are on the same file separated by an odd number of squares. } 8... Kb4 (8... Kc4 9. Kc2 Kd5 10. Kc3 Ke5 11. Kc4 Kd6 12. Kc3 Kd5 13. Kd3) 9. Kb2 Kc4 10. Kc2 { And now we can prevent black from entering the key squares with direct opposition. } *


