{ The white king occupies the key squares in front of the pawn, but how do we outflank the black king? This is possible thanks to a reserve move with the pawn. }
8. g4 Kh7 (8... Kg8 9. Kg6 Kh8 10. g5 Kg8 11. Kh6 Kh8 12. g6 Kg8) 9. Kf6 Kh8 (9... Kh6 10. g5+ Kh7 11. Kf7) 10. Kg6 Kg8 11. g5 { Another critical reserve move to force black out of opposition. } 11... Kh8 12. Kf7 Kh7 13. g6+ Kh8 14. g7+ Kh7 *


